---
description: Testing conventions — Jest unit/integration tests and Cypress end-to-end tests
globs: **/*.spec.ts,**/*.spec.tsx,**/*.test.ts,**/*.test.tsx,**/*.cy.ts,apps/frontend-e2e/**
---

# Jest:

- Write isolated, deterministic unit tests.
- Use descriptive test names and structure tests with `describe` and `it` blocks.
- Target 80% unit coverage, 100% on critical paths, and test all edge cases.
- Use factory functions for test data; avoid stale fixtures.
- Mock only external dependencies (APIs, DB). Never mock internal logic — tests should reflect reality, and over-mocking hides real bugs.
- Prefer functional test helpers and avoid test classes.

# Cypress:

- Write end-to-end tests that reflect real user flows.
- Use data-testid attributes for selectors.
- Keep tests independent and idempotent.
- Use custom Cypress commands for repeated actions.
- Prefer clear, step-by-step assertions.
